WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.667
So this job's all wrapped up.

00:00:01.707 --> 00:00:03.373
I'm here with Brett, the homeowner.

00:00:03.413 --> 00:00:05.080
Tell us how everything went, Brett.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.263
Mate, very impressed.

00:00:06.303 --> 00:00:09.023
Initially, when the insurance came out, it

00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:12.968
became a real hard thing

00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:13.544
to do.

00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:15.560
The insurance made us want to jump

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.040
through about 50 million hoops.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.723
We ended up dealing with it ourselves.

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:23.566
Rang Ethan from Top Tin, spoke to

00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:26.409
Vik originally, great guy to talk to,

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:28.885
put us in contact, told us what

00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:30.443
we needed to do, gave us an

00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:32.000
estimate up front, which was really, really

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.120
handy for us, especially for the

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.200
insurance and the process.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.763
Once Ethan came out on site and

00:00:38.803 --> 00:00:39.880
met me, I was sold.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:40.560
Very professional.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.940
The boys did a great job, very

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.792
accommodating, worked in with the solar guys

00:00:45.832 --> 00:00:47.520
and so on.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.400
Pointed out a few problems with the

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.280
roof that I wasn't even aware of.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.625
As far as the workmanship, the quality

00:00:53.665 --> 00:00:55.970
and the finish of the job, it

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.640
was absolutely fantastic.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.600
I couldn't recommend them enough.
